# Project rules

The application's requirements are not defined yet. Do not introduce architecture
(databases, auth, APIs, state libraries, folder conventions) ahead of an agreed plan.

## Commands

- `npm run dev` — local dev server
- `npm run lint` / `npm run typecheck` / `npm run test` / `npm run format:check`
- `npm run format` — apply Prettier formatting
- `npm run check` — every check plus a production build; this is the gate for all changes

## Working agreement

- Plan first. For anything beyond a trivial fix, propose the approach and wait for approval.
- Keep changes small and focused on one concern; no drive-by refactors or reformatting.
- Do not add, upgrade, or remove dependencies without approval. Pin exact versions.
- Do not commit, push, merge, deploy, or rewrite Git history unless explicitly asked.
- Work on a branch, never directly on `main`.
- Work is not done until `npm run check` exits 0. Report actual results, including failures.
- Add or update tests alongside behavior changes.
- Update `README.md` or this file when commands, setup, or conventions change.

## Secure coding

- Treat all external input (forms, URL params, headers, API bodies) as untrusted; validate
  it on the server before use. Client-side validation is for UX only.{% if zod %}
- Validate external input with the Zod schemas in `src/lib/schemas/`, which client and server
  code share. Add a schema and a test for every new input shape, and parse with `safeParse` at
  the trust boundary.{% if forms %}
- Build forms with React Hook Form and `zodResolver`, using the shared schema as the single source
  of the rules (see `src/components/forms/example-form.tsx`). Keep labels, `aria-invalid` and
  error messages linked, and test with a DOM environment (`// @vitest-environment jsdom`).{% endif %}{% if rest_api %}
- API v1 is additive-only: add optional fields, endpoints or error codes, never rename, remove or
  tighten anything (that needs `/api/v2`). Put each request and response shape in
  `src/lib/schemas/v1/`, `safeParse` every input, validate every response against its schema, and
  report errors with `problem()` from `src/server/api/responses.ts`. Server code stays in
  `src/server/` and `src/app/api/`; a test fails if a client component reaches it. See `docs/api-v1.md`.{% endif %}{% if has_database %}
- Database access is server-only: modules in `src/server/db/` and `src/server/items/` start with
  `import "server-only"`, use parameterized SQL only, and are never imported by client components{% if auth %}
  or, for the pool and transactions, by route handlers{% else %} or (until
  authentication exists) by route handlers{% endif %}. Change the schema only by adding a migration in
  `supabase/migrations/` (never edit a committed one) and running `npm run db:lock`. Validate every input
  with a Zod schema from `src/lib/schemas/`, pass `tx` from `withTransaction` to every call that belongs to a
  transaction, and never log a connection string. See `docs/database.md`.{% endif %}{% if auth %}
- Authentication is Better Auth in `src/server/auth/`. A route that needs a user is wrapped in
  `withAuthentication`; data of a user is read and written only through `withPrincipal` and a repository
  that takes its scope (never a user id from the request). The application's database role is
  `app_runtime`: never run it as the owner, never grant it more than a table needs, and give every table
  that holds user data an `owner_id` with row level security. Never disable the origin or CSRF checks, trust
  a client-supplied header for the client address, commit a secret, or answer 403 where a missing resource
  (404) would not reveal that it exists. See `docs/auth.md`.{% endif %}{% endif %}
- Enforce authorization on the server, close to the data, never only in the UI.
- Keep secrets in environment variables; never commit them, log them, or expose them to
  the browser (only `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables reach the client — never put secrets there).
- Return only the fields the caller needs; do not pass raw database or internal objects to
  Client Components or API responses.
- Prefer framework and platform features over hand-rolled security (crypto, sessions,
  escaping). Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/data-security.md` before
  writing data access or mutations.
